# Wave I.7 — Bundle isolation: admin host install classification

## Problem

Thin-shell claims on `apps/web` conflict with the **install graph**:

1. `@app-tour/workspace-starter` still sat in **`dependencies`** while denali/urban/guest-club lived in `devDependencies` — dual classification for the same product class.
2. `guard:host-workspace-deps` (Wave I.0) only blocked **orphans** (declared ∉ manifests). It did **not** require the admin transpile product set to be declared, nor forbid product packages in `dependencies`.

True `optionalDependencies` / filtered installs remain unsafe in this monorepo (dynamic `import("@app-tour/workspace-…")` must resolve). Bundle isolation’s honest next peel is **classification + completeness**, not pretending packages are absent.

## Decision

1. Move `@app-tour/workspace-starter` from `apps/web` `dependencies` → `devDependencies` (same class as other product workspaces).
2. Extend [`scripts/guards/guard-host-workspace-deps.mjs`](../../scripts/guards/guard-host-workspace-deps.mjs):

| Check | Host | Rule |
| ----- | ---- | ---- |
| Orphan | web + api | declared product dep ∉ any manifest `package` → fail (I.0) |
| Classification | **web only** | any product `@app-tour/workspace-*` (≠ sdk) in `dependencies` → fail |
| Completeness | **web only** | every package from `collectAdminProductTranspilePackages(manifests)` must appear in deps/devDeps/optionalDeps |

3. Keep IgnorePlugin + `ALLOW_*_WEB_PLUGIN` (Wave H.j) — client graph gate is orthogonal to install classification.

## Out of scope

- Moving products to `optionalDependencies` / removing IgnorePlugin
- Rewriting `apps/api` product deps into `devDependencies` (API loads handlers at runtime)
- Requiring **all** manifest packages on web (finance registry-only stay off the product trunk)
- Codegen rewrite of web `package.json` product keys → [`wave-i-8-admin-web-product-deps.mdoc`](./wave-i-8-admin-web-product-deps.mdoc) (Wave I.8)

## Status

**DONE** — starter reclassified; host guard ratchets classification + admin-transpile completeness.

## Verify

```bash
pnpm run guard:host-workspace-deps
pnpm run wave-i0:guard
pnpm --filter @apps/web exec node --import tsx --test \
  test/wave-i-7-host-install-classification.spec.ts
```

## PSR-4b-api-deps extension (2026-07-31)

API host now also requires **completeness**: every `workspace.manifest.json`
`package` must be declared on `apps/api/package.json` (exact set with orphan
check). See [`psr-4b-api-deps.mdoc`](../audits/snapshots/2026-07-31/psr-4b-api-deps.mdoc).
Codegen rewrite of API `package.json` remains deferred (`PSR-4b-api-deps-sync`).

